{"entries":[{"id":"tsk-jhn-6-1","title":"John 6:1","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JHN","chapterStart":6,"verseStart":1,"chapterEnd":6,"verseEnd":1},"content":"<p>1 Christ feeds five thousand men with five loaves and two fishes. 15 Thereupon the people would have made him king; 16 but withdrawing himself, he walks on the sea to his disciples; 26 reproves the people flocking after him, and all the fleshly hearers of his word; 32 declares himself to be the bread of life to believers. 66 Many disciples depart from him. 68 Peter confesses him. 70 Judas is a devil.</p>\n<p>A.M. 4036. A.D. 32. these. Mt 14:13,15-21; Mr 6:31,32,34,35-44; Lu 9:10-12,13-17 the sea. Nu 34:11; Jos 12:3; Mt 4:18; 15:29; Lu 5:1 which. 23; 21:1</p>"},{"id":"tsk-jhn-6-2","title":"John 6:2","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JHN","chapterStart":6,"verseStart":2,"chapterEnd":6,"verseEnd":2},"content":"<p>Mt 4:24,25; 8:1; 12:15; 13:2; 14:14; 15:30,31; Mr 6:33</p>"},{"id":"tsk-jhn-6-3","title":"John 6:3","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JHN","chapterStart":6,"verseStart":3,"chapterEnd":6,"verseEnd":3},"content":"<p>15; Mt 14:23; 15:29; Lu 6:12,13; 9:28</p>"},{"id":"tsk-jhn-6-4","title":"John 6:4","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JHN","chapterStart":6,"verseStart":4,"chapterEnd":6,"verseEnd":4},"content":"<p>2:13; 5:1; 11:55; 12:1; 13:1; Ex 12:6-14; Le 23:5,7; De 16:1</p>"},{"id":"tsk-jhn-6-5","title":"John 6:5","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JHN","chapterStart":6,"verseStart":5,"chapterEnd":6,"verseEnd":5},"content":"<p>saw. 4:35; Mt 14:14,15; Mr 6:34,35; Lu 9:12 Whence. Mt 15:33; Mr 8:2-4; Lu 9:13</p>"},{"id":"tsk-jhn-6-6","title":"John 6:6","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)","reference":{"book":"JHN","chapterStart":6,"verseStart":6,"chapterEnd":6,"verseEnd":6},"content":"<p>prove. Ge 22:1; De 8:2,16; 13:3; 33:8; 2Ch 32:31</p>"},{"id":"tsk-jhn-6-7","title":"John 6:7","author":"R. A. Torrey (editor)